{"manifest":{"slug":"north-alabama-mental-health-systems","title":"North Alabama Mental Health Systems Report","short_title":"North Alabama Mental Health","subtitle":"A descriptive analysis of the mental health system of systems in Madison and Cullman counties and the fifteen-county Huntsville crisis catchment, for advocates, planners and coalition partners","question":"What does the mental health system of systems look like in WellStone's service area in October 2026 (who decides, who pays, what exists, who delivers it, who is reached and who is missed) in Madison and Cullman counties, and how does the wider fifteen-county crisis catchment depend on it?","as_of":"2026-10-04","authors":["Little Orange Fish, prepared with Claude"],"venue":"DRAFT FOR REVIEW. Not approved by Little Orange Fish and not peer reviewed. Researched and written with Claude from public sources on 4 October 2026; awaiting review by Little Orange Fish.","year":2026,"report":{"publisher":"Little Orange Fish, Huntsville, Alabama","version":"v261004.1","status":"draft-for-review","companion":"Alabama Mental Health Systems Report, v261003.1","independence":"Independent of WellStone and of every organization described; public sources only; none supplied material, saw the text or endorsed it."},"plain_abstract":"WellStone is the public mental health center for Madison and Cullman counties, and its crisis center in Huntsville is assigned people from fifteen. This report describes the system around it in one place: who governs and pays, what services exist, who staffs them, what is measured, who is reached and who is missed, and how schools, courts, jails, housing and insurers shape the result. It follows the eight domains and four cross-sector sections of the statewide Alabama Mental Health Systems Report, applied to two counties in depth and to the thirteen surrounding counties in outline. It was researched and written with Claude from public sources only, and every sentence was read back against the passage that supports it. You can read the report with each sentence's source one hover away and see what could not be read, confirmed or found. It is a draft for review, independent of WellStone, and not an approved or peer-reviewed publication.","reading_minutes":92,"audience":"advocates, planners and coalition partners in north Alabama; assumes no background in health policy","palette":{"groups":{"domain":"#e8762b","cross_sector":"#3f6f8f","core":"#e8762b","ring":"#7a8791","verified":"#2e7d5b","changed":"#b3541e","open":"#9a6b00"}},"permissions":{"text":"Report text written for Little Orange Fish with Claude and published here as a draft for review; source summaries written for this site; no third-party text reproduced beyond quotations of 25 words or fewer, each attributed and cited.","figures":"Charts, maps and the systems graph are built for this site from cited public data; no published figure images are reproduced. The Little Orange Fish logo is used with the publisher's permission."},"github_account":"feelingsarereal","notes_storage":"file","builder":{"name":"Manuscript Interrogator","version":"0.5.2","date":"2026-10-04"},"banner":{"text":"Draft for review. This report has not been approved by Little Orange Fish, is independent of WellStone and every organization it describes, and is not a position of the North Alabama Mental Health Coalition or its members. It was researched and written with Claude from public sources; every sentence was read back against its source on 4 October 2026, and the open items show what could not be settled.","links":[{"label":"Open items","to":"/open-items"},{"label":"How it was made","to":"/methods"}]},"draft":true},"brand":{"organisation":"Little Orange Fish","address":"101 Quality Circle, Suite 140, Huntsville, Alabama 35806","email":"info@littleorangefish.org","website":"littleorangefish.org","tagline":"A strong community is built of healthy individuals, and good health starts with a healthy mind.","logo":"brand/little-oran