and a safe place for help all now exist in Huntsville, and no published count shows how many people they have kept out of a jail or an emergency room."},{"id":"eight-domains","title":"The eight domains","one_liner":"The report asks of Madison and Cullman counties the same questions the statewide report asks of Alabama, in eight domains and four cross-sector sections, and adds one section of its own on the ring."},{"id":"how-local-mental-health-is-funded","title":"How local mental health is funded","one_liner":"The public system in Madison and Cullman counties is paid for by state appropriations, Medicaid, federal grants, local governments, settlement money and gifts, and only some of those streams can be read to the dollar."},{"id":"how-this-report-was-made","title":"How this report was made","one_liner":"Facts were recorded with their supporting passages before any prose was written, and every block of the report was then read back against those passages by checkers that did not write it."},{"id":"medicaid-and-the-coverage-gap","title":"Medicaid and the coverage gap","one_liner":"Alabama has not expanded Medicaid, so many low-income adults cannot enroll, and a clinic that is paid its daily rate only for Medicaid enrollees must still serve everyone who comes."},{"id":"reading-the-numbers","title":"Reading the numbers","one_liner":"Before comparing two figures in this report, check what each one counts, who published it, which period it covers and how many events lie behind it."},{"id":"sequential-intercept-model","title":"The Sequential Intercept Model","one_liner":"Six points between a crisis and community supervision at which a person with mental illness can be turned toward care; in Madison and Cullman counties most of what stands at each point is known by its launch date and by little else."},{"id":"three-maps","title":"One service area, three maps","one_liner":"WellStone is the mental health center for two counties and the crisis center for fifteen, and \"Region 1\" names three other areas, so a regional figure means little until its map is known."},{"id":"workforce-shortage-measures","title":"Measuring the workforce shortage","one_liner":"A federal designation, a provider ratio and a count of beds that cannot be staffed answer different questions, and in Madison and Cullman counties they give different answers."}],"figures":[{"id":"fig-two-counties","label":"Figure 1","title":"Madison and Cullman counties side by side, with Alabama","kind":"table"},{"id":"fig-commitments","label":"Figure 2","title":"What has been said in public about commitments in Madison County","kind":"table"},{"id":"fig-access","label":"Figure 3","title":"Days a new patient waited at WellStone, January and December 2025","kind":"table"},{"id":"fig-served","label":"Figure 4","title":"Four published figures for WellStone in fiscal year 2025","kind":"chart"},{"id":"fig-housing","label":"Figure 5","title":"People counted as homeless and supportive housing beds, Huntsville continuum, 2022 to 2025","kind":"chart"},{"id":"fig-systems-graph","label":"Figure 6","title":"How the parts of the regional system depend on one another","kind":"network"}],"layersBrief":[{"id":"pop_est","label":"Population estimate","geography":["county"],"panel_only":false},{"id":"pct_under18","label":"Persons under 18 years","geography":["county"],"panel_only":false},{"id":"pct_65plus","label":"Persons 65 years and over","geography":["county"],"panel_only":false},{"id":"pct_black","label":"Black alone","geography":["county"],"panel_only":false},{"id":"pct_hispanic","label":"Hispanic or Latino","geography":["county"],"panel_only":false},{"id":"pct_white_nh","label":"White alone, not Hispanic or Latino","geography":["county"],"panel_only":false},{"id":"pct_aian","label":"American Indian and Alaska Native alone","geography":["county"],"panel_only":false},{"id":"veterans","label":"Veterans","geography":["county"],"panel_only":false},{"id":"median_hh_income","label":"Median household inc